============================================================
  SCALABILITY NOTE
============================================================

  The H computation is O(2^n * n^2) via Hamiltonian path DP.
  Practical limits:
    n <= 15: instant (< 1 second)
    n <= 20: feasible (< 1 minute)
    n <= 25: possible with optimization (< 1 hour)
    n > 25: use Copeland ranking + approximate Q score

  For large n, the Copeland ranking captures 96-97%% of the
  information (OCR theorem). The quality score Q can be
  approximated from the score sequence alone.

  APPROXIMATE Q FOR LARGE n:
    Q_approx = 1 - c3 / C(n,3)
    where c3 = number of 3-cycles (computable in O(n^3))
    This captures the dominant source of ranking ambiguity.
